        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add details of support added in Firefox 144 for the ability to determine the precedence of injected CSS through the  <a href=\"http://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/manifest.json/content_scripts\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">\"content_scripts\"</code> manifest key</a>, in <a href=\"http://developer.mozilla.orgdeveloper.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/API/scripting/registerContentScripts\" rel=\"nofollow\">scripting.registerContentScripts()</a> with the <code class=\"notranslate\">cssOrigin</code> property on <a href=\"http://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/API/scripting/RegisteredContentScript\" rel=\"nofollow\">scripting.RegisteredContentScript</a>, and the <code class=\"notranslate\">cssOrigin</code> property in <a href=\"http://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/API/contentScripts/register\" rel=\"nofollow\">contentScripts.register</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Addresses the dev-docs-needed requirements of <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1679997\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1679997</a> Add cssOrigin to declarative contentScripts API (manifest.json, scripting, contentScripts)</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">MDN documentation provided in TBC</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27716",
            "title": "Bug-1679997 CSS origin for registered content scripts",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-02T16:42:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-31T17:59:00.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is a bit of a test PR to see if we could add spec_urls everywhere (especially for behavioral sub features).<br>\nSome things came up where we should probably agree on spec_url consistency for a few common sub features:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>worker_support</li>\n<li>iterable sub features (forEach, keys, values, iterator, etc)</li>\n<li>secure_context_required<br>\nI decided to use the spec_url for the interface itself, happy to hear other thoughts.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, I think when a sub aspect of e.g. a method is described then it is okay to link to the same spec section as the method. So, basically the sub feature gets the same spec_url as the parent feature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I marked standard_track false for a few things: CSSPrimitiveValue, CSSValue, CSSValueList, DOMError, FeaturePolicy. Doesn't look like these will be going anywhere.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27671",
            "title": "Add more spec_urls; set some standard_tracks to false (APIs A-E)",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-02T09:41:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-26T13:10:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates MDN browser compatibility data for the Meta Quest Browser (Oculus). The data was collected using the <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"organization\" data-hovercard-url=\"/orgs/openwebdocs/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs\">@openwebdocs</a> BCD collector project using a Meta Quest 2 device. Additional sources:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Release dates: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Quest_Browser\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Quest_Browser</a><br>\nRelease notes: <a href=\"https://developers.meta.com/horizon/release-notes/web\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developers.meta.com/horizon/release-notes/web</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/jacobrossi/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/jacobrossi\">@jacobrossi</a> <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/cabanier/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/cabanier\">@cabanier</a> <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/davehill00/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/davehill00\">@davehill00</a>, would anyone of you be interested in helping to review this data?</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27556",
            "title": "Update Meta Quest (Oculus) data",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-11T11:09:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-11T11:06:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">picker-icon</code> CSS selector. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.14.0).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/selectors/picker-icon\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/selectors/picker-icon</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27546",
            "title": "Chrome 133 already added `::picker-icon` CSS pseudo-element",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-14T18:07:55.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-09T19:24:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">checkmark</code> CSS selector. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.14.0).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/selectors/checkmark\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/selectors/checkmark</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27545",
            "title": "Chrome 133 already added `::checkmark` CSS pseudo-element",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-14T18:08:34.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-09T19:23:11.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36379249?u=4840c2d79361800483d4c22b03d928ae33115103&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As discussed in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18\" rel=\"nofollow\">Mozilla Bug 1316857 comment 18</a>, the concept of \"same script\" is vague and likely inaccurate.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Additionally, to determine script-closeability, browsers switched from 'has an opener' to 'was opened by script' and that might be useful to note.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"834043421\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/9492\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/9492/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/9492\">#9492</a></p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My perception is these notes are usually quite short. Script-closeability also depends on the session history, so something like \"Before Chrome 95, scripts could only close windows that had an opener\" would be incorrect. I tried to omit this detail, but am unsure whether that made my phrasing too awkward. We could remove the notes entirely. An alternative phrasing might be \"Before Chrome 95, whether a window could be closed by script depended on having an opener, not on whether it was created by web content.\"</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27396",
            "title": "Chrome 95 / FF 128 add script-closeability depending on opener",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-19T07:39:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-24T14:09:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "vinhill",
                "url": "https://github.com/vinhill"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for all browsers for the <code class=\"notranslate\">global_attributes</code> SVG feature. This replaces a majority of ranges within the SVG global attributes by copying data from the CSS property counterparts.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27389",
            "title": "Update all browsers data for global_attributes SVG feature",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-19T18:17:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-23T17:33:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for all browsers for the <code class=\"notranslate\">text-orientation</code> CSS property. The data comes from manual testing, running test code through BrowserStack, SauceLabs, custom VMs and/or locally.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Test Code:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"\n(Using bcd.testCSSProperty() from the collector)\n\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">\n(Using bcd.testCSSProperty() from the collector)\n\n</code></pre></div>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27189",
            "title": "Update all browsers data for text-orientation CSS property",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-11T16:54:23.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-30T05:02:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">speak</code> CSS property. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.13.3).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/properties/speak\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/properties/speak</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27188",
            "title": "Chrome 8 added `speak` CSS property",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-22T16:43:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-30T04:36:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Based on <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1140067250\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15006\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006\">#15006</a>.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds the <code class=\"notranslate\">abort</code> event on <code class=\"notranslate\">IDBDatabase</code>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The IDBDatabase abort event is defined in the spec, and implemented in Chrome, Firefox, and Safari, so the data shouldn't<br>\nhave been removed in the first place.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-important\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-report mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 1.75C0 .784.784 0 1.75 0h12.5C15.216 0 16 .784 16 1.75v9.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.25 13H8.06l-2.573 2.573A1.458 1.458 0 0 1 3 14.543V13H1.75A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25Zm1.75-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v9.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h2a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.19l2.72-2.72a.749.749 0 0 1 .53-.22h6.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-9.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25Zm7 2.25v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 9a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z\"></path></svg>Important</p><p dir=\"auto\">While the same <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345#issuecomment-3024294352\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345/hovercard\">may apply to 50+ events</a> that can bubble to Element, Document, and Window, we do <strong>not</strong> intend to add corresponding data to those three interfaces.</p>\n</div>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The data was originally removed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1140067250\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15006\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006\">#15006</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #15345.\">Fixes</span>: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1166786936\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345\">#15345</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27167",
            "title": "Re-add IDBDatabase abort event",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-03T09:57:49.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-27T14:00:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 136 adds support to the MediaRecorder API for HEVC encoding, introducing the hvc1.* codec string, and adds new codecs (hev1.* and avc3.*) supporting variable resolution video in MP4. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6375884229181440\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6375884229181440</a> for more details.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for this support to the <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaRecorder()</code> constructor, and to the <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaRecorder.isTypeSupported()</code> static method.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaRecorder.mimeType</code> property is also related, but it only returns a previously-set value rather than setting a MIME type, so I decided to not add a data point there.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27142",
            "title": "Add data points for Chrome 136 MediaRecorder H26x codec support",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-22T15:47:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-25T14:32:03.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        }
    ]
